<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="fatty acid β-oxidation III (unsaturated, odd number)" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-5137" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: This pathway is on the list of Common Viridiplantae Pathways (CVP) generated for the COMET project, which includes pathways that are thought to be present in all or most Viridiplantae species including algae. All UPP pathways are automatically imported into databases regardless of Pathologic predictions. &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; When fatty acids that contain a &lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-double bond on odd-numbered carbons are processed by |FRAME: CPLX-7064| (see |FRAME: PWY-5136|), they are converted to |FRAME: CIS-DELTA3-ENOYL-COA|. These compounds must be converted to |FRAME: TRANS-D2-ENOYL-COA| before they can be processed further |CITS: [11755682]|. Monofunctional proteins having such activity have been described from many organisms, including mammals, plants and bacteria. In plants, this activity is also a part of of the multifunction protein (MFP) (see |FRAME: MONOMER-12057|, |FRAME: MONOMER-12058|, |FRAME: MONOMER-12059|).</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="xue" />
    <Author name="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE" />
    <Author name="zhang" />
  </Authors>
